Pros:
+ Shadowrun universe. That means it's possible to play as an elf decker wielding a sniper rifle;
+ Next logical step from Shadowrun: Dragonfall;
+ Matrix is now like "use stealth and have a good memory". I really liked that;
+ Characters have really good depth and it was fun talking to them in-between missions;
+ Some UI screens were changed, such as the skill tree and the "I don't have space to get this item" screen;
+ Etiquettes and special options appeared way more often in dialogs. Thank you HBS!;
Cons:
- Too much consecutive time reading. I like it wordy, but sometimes I'd skip dialogues for being too tired;
- Still too linear and each map has only a few points of interest;
- I could't get money to buy more than one implant. I played as a Decker and everytime I could I'd buy a new deck and programs. Apparently the best strategy is to skip such purchases and make them when your skills are maxed. Still, I couldn't even afford to buy equipments to my party and there's no other way of getting money. Dragonfall was very different in that regard, since I managed to get implants in all slots;
- Most of the achievements unlocked are the same as previous versions. I felt it was a little sloppy.

