I have spent way too much time on this thing, but every hour was well worth it!
If you like strategies, especially 4Xs than this is a must have and because it's cheap you can get friends to play with you.
That aside, I'm just going to briefly run through pros and cons:
Cons:
- Bad AI, which is why online games are way more fun; you can engage in some real diplomacy;
- Clumsy warfare system; moving tons of units, every one of them independently could hardly be more irritating;
Pros:
- Veeeery engaging! I simply love seeing my emire grow and prosper;
- Great city management with interesting options for growth;
- Varied ways to win the game, which lead to situations where your soliders refuse to kill off the reamining player as he's sold you "too much pop music and jeans";
- Hot seat, while takes a lot of time, it is great to play with someone in the same room.
Overall, I'd recomment trying Civ to everybody, I've played it both with friends and family and they all very much enjoyed it!

